From 55f52a9506bd2016f4f850e6443abdbb1a3e7269 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:23:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] test a real sync-loop process publishes its held
 claim record before its first round
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Post-merge audit t_01a1d839f0aa6622 of PR #2715 (landed 9435baf78d, owner t_01a1d6c4e700958e) found that
`hermes_cli/kanban_sync_claims.py:176` `temp.replace(target)` -> `temp.unlink()` (the held record is never
published) survives all 111 tests of the claim-gate / sync-client / singleton-lease family with zero skips. The
split-process tests hand-write the `.sync-claims.json` record themselves, so nothing checks that a real loop
produces it, and the after-stop "record absent" assertion is vacuous when no record was ever written.

New test: a child process runs the real `kanban_sync_stop.run_loop` (loop_started -> _write, note_round,
loop_stopped) and pauses inside its first round. This process has no sync loop (a profile gateway's dispatcher
or a shell `hermes kanban claim`) and must:
- defer the claim during that initial sync (real `dispatch_once`: claim_deferred sync_first_round, card ready),
- claim once the producer's round reaches the head (record lists the board open),
- see the record removed after the producer's tenure ends.

Test-only change; no production code touched.

Mutation proof (sdlc-review mutants.py, 3-file family claim_gate + sync_client + singleton_lease, scratch
HOME/HERMES_HOME, no board env pins):
- kanban_sync_claims.py:176 persist omitted: killed (was SURVIVED on 111 tests)
- loop_stopped unlink omitted: killed
- _write "open" always {}: killed
- control: gateway/kanban_watchers.py:469 loop_expected() omitted (sibling gap t_01a1d87d1a960fd1): survives this
  family, as predicted — owned separately.

Card: t_01a1d87d194d4887
